      "content": "a drinking-vessel, formerly made of wooden staves and hooped; now esp. a tall one-handled jug or mug, usually of pewter, sometimes with a lid: used chiefly for drinking beer (OED s.v. tankard 2a) (see also drynkyng tankerd) | drinking glass"
